'''SoL''': [[Cave Fillet|Sub-chapter 7 - Cave Fillet]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[1 + 2 = Tor|Sub-chapter 8 - 1 + 2 = Tor]]
|money drop = 8,000¢ - 31,600¢
}}

==Enemy==
Teacher Bun Bun is by far the toughest opponent faced in Empire of Cats, with much higher health and more pushing power than any previously encountered enemy, due to his rapid, short-ranged area attacks and high speed. He can and will destroy nearly anything that enters his range (200) - that includes [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]].

He may seem unbeatable, but he '''can''' be defeated with the proper strategy, an example being [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cats]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] stacked in tandem with a continuous spam of "[[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]]" (e.g., [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]], [[Coin Cat (Special Cat)|Coin Cat]], [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Samba Cat]], etc) to delay and absorb his hits.

==Strategy==
It is highly recommended to get all Superior [[Treasure]]s in all Empire of Cats Chapters (prioritize the [[Energy Drink]], [[Giant Safe]], [[Relativity Clock]], [[Super Register]], [[Legendary Cat Shield]], and [[Legendary Cat Sword]]) to make him manageable, along with upgrading every cat you're using to level 20. See [[Moon (Empire of Cats)]] for more in-depth information.

Take advantage of his short reach and prioritize long-ranged attackers over tanks; Mythical Titan Cat can only take so many hits from him, but a gang of Dragon Cats and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]] can deal massive damage given enough time at a range advantage. [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating units]] with slow, freeze or weaken abilities like [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]] are quite helpful, provided they have enough range to land a hit on him. Even so, he is beatable without their assistance.

Later on, Teacher Bun Bun and most of his variants' pushing power decrease drastically despite their bulk and brute strength, due to the player having faster meatshields, like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]], and powerful anti-Floating [[True Form]]s such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] to cripple them.

However, once you reach [[Uncanny Legends]] and especially on 2- and 3-Crown difficulties, Bun Bun variants can truly become actual monsters, as their health skyrockets to where it's much harder to kill them quickly and they are often supported by backliners or other strong pushers, though they still retain their weakness of having very short range. Take advantage of your specialists and Crowd-Controllers, especially [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] and units obtained later on such as [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]].

