==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = Teacher Bun Bun
|J.K. Bun Bun
|Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant. Slightly smaller in aesthetic size. Stats are only slightly more than a 400% Teacher Bun Bun, but he has half the number of knockbacks.
|Bun Bun Black
|Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] variant. Bigger in aesthetic size. Superior health, but has less speed and attack power than a 400% Bun Bun, as well as the same number of knockbacks.
|Bun Bun Symbiote
|Teacher Bun Bun's [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant. Slightly bigger than Bun Bun Black. Has superior health & attack power, with half as many knockbacks and a 5% chance to create a Lv. 1 [[Wave Attack|Wave]].
|Li'l Bun Bun
|A much smaller variant of Teacher Bun Bun. Has lower health, attack power and range, but is much faster, gets knocked back half as many times, drops less money and appears in swarms along with extreme buffs.
|Mecha-Bun
|The final boss of [[Stories of Legend]], a visually mechanical variant of Teacher Bun Bun piloted by a [[Doge]]. Has a gigantic amount of health and damage, a faster attack rate, and piercing Omni Strikes. Despite having Mecha in its name, it's not considered a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy and keeps the Floating trait. After clearing its debut stage, [[Eldritch Forces]], Mecha-Bun is unlocked as a [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Mythic Cat]].
|Relic Bun-Bun
|Mecha-Bun's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant. Attacks even faster, gets knocked back half as many times, has even longer reach, deals half as much damage, moves slower, and is guaranteed to [[Curse|curse]] Cat Units for 10 seconds. Once its debut stage ([[An Ancient Curse]]) is cleared, Mecha-Bun's True Form becomes available. Unlike most other variants, Relic Bun-Bun is '''not''' a Floating enemy.
|Commander Bun Bun
|A Teacher Bun Bun variant introduced in 12th Anniversary stages. Has higher health and attack power and Omni Strikes that extend up to 280 range.
|Xenobeast Bunaglios
|An Alien/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] introduced in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Hunt for the Xenobeast]]. Behaves rather differently from other Bun Buns, with a slower attack rate and animation, unusually long range (400 standing, 450 Omni Strike), a guaranteed [[Explosion]] that spawns at 400 range and a 20% [[Critical Hit|Critical]] chance. Surprisingly, Xenobeast Bunaglios is also '''not''' a Floating enemy.
}}

