==Trivia==
*Teacher Bun Bun may be named after the prefix ぶん ''bun-'', which emphasizes the following verb or indicates doing something with force, or ぷんぷん ''punpun'', which can mean either "pungent" or "angry" (e.g., [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/geki-oko-punpun-maru Geki Oko Punpun Maru]). This would explain he and his variants' general association with violence.
*"Don't think. FEEL!" is a quote by [[wikipedia:Bruce Lee|Bruce Lee]]'s character in the movie ''[[wikipedia:Enter the Dragon|Enter the Dragon]]'', Lee.
*Each Yuki [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] from the [[Shoumetsu Toshi Collaboration Event|Shoumetsu Toshi]] collab attacks with a different Bun Bun. Teacher Bun Bun appears in [[Mystery Girl Yuki (Uber Rare Cat)|Mystery Girl Yuki]]'s attack animation; [[Bun Bun Black]] appears in [[Crazed Yuki (Uber Rare Cat)|Crazed Yuki]]'s attack animation; and [[J.K. Bun Bun]] appears in [[Lost World Yuki (Uber Rare Cat)|Lost World Yuki]]'s attack animation.
*[[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Superstar Koneko]] and [[Metal Maiden Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Metal Maiden Koneko]] are protected by security guards Teacher Bun Bun and Bun Bun Black, respectively.
**Given the Bun Buns' gargoyle-like appearances, this may be a reference to how gargoyles were believed to protect against evil.
*[[The Face]], [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and Teacher Bun Bun all share the same amount of health: 99,999. However, Nyandam only has [[Soul Leasing|one unbuffed appearance]], and Teacher Bun Bun has always been fought at 400% or more.
*He is the only [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] boss without an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant.
*[[Crustaceous Scissorex]]'s shell appears to be a Bun Bun's skull. This is further confirmed by the former's description mentioning its acquisition of Teacher Bun Bun's "irrational power of love".
*It seems there may be a power struggle of sorts within the Bun Bun family, as seen in the stage [[Trouble at the Mansion]] (which contains a Teacher Bun Bun and numerous Li'l Bun Buns). The term ''Oiesōdō'' (お家騒動) in the stage's Japanese name, Bukeyashiki Oiesōdō (武家屋敷お家騒動, "Family Trouble at the Samurai Mansion"), literally means "family trouble" or "domestic trouble", but could also refer to an internal squabble (over headship rights) in a daimyo family during the Edo period of Japan.
*The "Love" in [[Don't Rush Love]] may be the same "love" from Teacher Bun Bun's description.
*One of the possible endings for [[Gamatoto Expedition]] log messages is "with Teacher Bun-Bun."
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Teacher Bun Bun is heavily nerfed, with his attack cycle lasting for five seconds, though J.K. Bun Bun and Bun Bun Black are left untouched.
*From [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] to [[Version 5.9 Update|Version 5.9]], Teacher Bun Bun was a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy.

